AKATH_CORE/runtime/runtime-registry.json
AKATH_CORE/runtime/runtime-state.json
AKATH_CORE/runtime/evidence.jsonl

# Vendored tooling (fetch with scripts/install-luau.sh)
tools/

# Credentials must never be committed. They live in OpenHands secrets and the KV
# vault, or on disk outside the repo (/workspace/.secrets, /workspace/ax-tools).
# ops/risk_audit.py fails the "secret_hygiene" check if these rules are missing.
.secrets/
**/.secrets/
*.pem
*.p12

# aeris938-1 pipeline: generated assets and renders are large; manifests are kept.
aeris938-1/work/
aeris938-1/library/img/*.png
aeris938-1/library/img/*.jpg
aeris938-1/library/music/*.mp3
aeris938-1/library/covers/*.png
!aeris938-1/library/*/manifest.json

# Python bytecode from the aeris938-1 pipeline
aeris938-1/**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
aeris938-1/dist/

# music938-1: generated audio, video, covers and caches are large; scripts,
# lyrics, tests and the manifests are tracked.
# Ignore the contents, not the directory: git cannot re-include a file inside an
# ignored directory, and the release ledger below must survive a clone.
music938-1/work/*
# The AI-written lyric candidates are the reviewable artifact for a re-render:
# keep them so K can read what will replace the current lyrics before it ships.
!music938-1/work/lyric-candidates/
!music938-1/work/lyric-candidates/**
# The release ledger is the only record of what is already on YouTube, and
# release.py writes it under work/. If it is ignored, a fresh clone re-uploads
# every song as a duplicate.
!music938-1/work/release-state.json
# market.py writes the daily channel report and its diff baseline here, and the
# market-daily automation commits them back so the next run can diff. Tracked on
# purpose: they are the loop's memory, not a build artifact.
!music938-1/work/market-report.md
!music938-1/work/market-snapshot.json
!music938-1/work/market-weekly-automation.json
# Same reason as the ledger: this is the list of clips that shipped broken and
# still need replacing, and it is only useful to a session that can read it.
!music938-1/work/pending-replacements.json
# The FB/TikTok rail's queue and posted-once ledger. The ledger is the only
# record of what is already on Reels/TikTok, so it must survive a recycle.
!music938-1/work/crosspost-queue.json
!music938-1/work/crosspost-state.json
# The response loop's memory: the last play-count per posted URL (so a run reads
# only new posts, not every post ever made) and the decision it drew (so the next
# run knows which format won). Without these the loop re-reads from scratch each
# run and cannot tell whether a change helped.
!music938-1/work/engagement-cache.json
!music938-1/work/engagement.json
# The release pin: songs K asked to publish next. The daily runner fetches `main`
# and only a tracked file reaches it, so an ignored pin would never fire. The pin
# is inert once the song's main release is live (see release.plan).
!music938-1/work/release-priority.json
# The playlist id per bucket. Without it a fresh clone would create a duplicate
# playlist on the first run instead of adding to the one that already exists.
!music938-1/work/playlist-state.json
# social_stats.py writes the FB/TikTok/Shopee numbers here. market.py covers
# YouTube only, so this is the loop's only view of the other three surfaces and
# must survive a recycle.
!music938-1/work/social-report.md
# The affiliate product cards. The rendered clips ship in the media release, but
# the source of truth for a *re-render* is this file — without it a fresh pod has
# no cards, make_affiliate_short cannot run, and its test fails on an empty list.
!music938-1/work/affiliate-products.json
# The compilation upload record. It is the guard that stops the monthly job from
# publishing a near-identical album every month — on a fresh CI checkout the file
# only exists if it is tracked, so an ignored state file means the guard never
# fires and the channel floods with duplicates.
!music938-1/work/compilation-state-*.json
# The mood-clip render record. Same reason as the compilation record: the `--once`
# guard only skips a re-render if the file survives a fresh CI checkout, so an
# ignored state file means all six clips re-render every 4 hours forever.
!music938-1/work/mood-clips-state.json
music938-1/library/songs/*.mp3
music938-1/library/songs/*.wav
music938-1/library/songs/*.m4a
music938-1/library/songs/stems-*/
music938-1/library/covers/*.png
music938-1/library/karaoke/*.mp4
!music938-1/library/*/manifest.json
music938-1/**/__pycache__/
# clip metadata is regenerable from Flow Music; keep the tree small
music938-1/library/songs/clipmeta-*.json

# Shorts, thumbnails and cover jpgs are regenerable renders; the durable copy
# lives in the GitHub Release (see the 24h release mechanism).
music938-1/library/shorts/*.mp4
music938-1/library/affiliate/*.mp4
# The absurdist "exhibit" clips (K's FB/TK rebrand) are regenerable ffmpeg
# renders over the covers we already own; the durable copy is the media release.
music938-1/library/surreal/*.mp4
# The real-instrument mood clips (K approved the six beds, 2026-11-09) are
# regenerable ffmpeg renders; the durable copy is the media release.
music938-1/library/moods/*.mp4
# The live-concert takes (K's "เสียงแสดงสด" lane) are regenerable ffmpeg renders
# of our own songs through the hall/PA/crowd mix; the durable copy is the release.
music938-1/library/concert/*.mp4
music938-1/library/thumbs/*.png
music938-1/library/covers/*.jpg
# The compilation render is a 200 MB+ artifact; keep the .txt/.title (chapters) but not the video.
music938-1/library/compilations/*.mp4
# The ambient beds are ffmpeg synth, regenerated on demand; only the sidecars ship.
# They are WAV now (sample-exact, so the loop crossfade is seamless), not MP3.
music938-1/library/ambient/*.mp3
music938-1/library/ambient/*.wav
# Local review pages; they point at multi-hundred-MB renders and are regenerated
# on demand when K wants to see a batch before it is published.
music938-1/library/preview.html
music938-1/library/ambient-preview.html
music938-1/library/surreal/preview.html

# Quarantined media is the rejected Piper engine, kept only for audit. Never
# publish it and never commit it (see scripts/provenance.py).
music938-1/library/quarantine/
ops/out/

# Scratch: K's source uploads, extracted frames and preview renders.
/work/

# The share pack: small files are committed, the audio is large and is not.
share/aeris-music/music/
share/aeris-music/covers/*.jpg
!share/aeris-music/beds/
!music938-1/work/produce-queue.json
# The YouTube shared-quota ledger. Every worker reads and writes it through the
# Contents API, so it must be tracked or the reservation is invisible to the rest.
!music938-1/work/yt-quota.json
